<title>JAPAN: Japan Jan copper cable shipments, orders up 7.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan Jan copper cable shipments, orders up 7.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese copper wire and cable shipments and orders rose a robust 7.1 percent in January from the same month last year, the Japanese Electric Wire and Cable Makers' Association said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The association said the rise in shipments to the telecommunications sector was fuelled by construction of new facilities for cellular phone services.</p>
<p>Demand also continued to show strong growth in the automobile and construction sectors, which were buoyed by low domestic interest rates and consumer purchases ahead of April's national sales tax hike, the association said.  </p>
<p>The preliminary January data and revised December data were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   Jan 97     yr/yr change	Dec 96 (revised)</p>
<p> Orders	  85,900	 +7.1 pct	  84,079  (-1.9 pct)</p>
<p>   Exports	4,200	-11,4 pct	   3,705  (-0.1 pct)</p>
<p> Shipments     86,900	 +7.1 pct	  85,972  (+0.8 pct)</p>
<p>   Constr'n    32,600	+15.1 pct	  33,861  (+5.3 pct)</p>
<p>   Electrical  22,900	 +2.2 pct	  22,780  (-1.1 pct)</p>
<p>   Elec Power  11,400	 +3.1 pct	   9,108 (-11.8 pct)</p>
<p>   Automobile   5,700	+19.0 pct	   6,298 (+20.8 pct)</p>
<p>   Telecomms    3,800	+16.1 pct	   3,077 (+12.7 pct)</p>
<p>   Exports	3,500	-17.0 pct	   3,900 (-17.6 pct)</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
